{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 182 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "fa0cea4fb87a7bfa62ab237fc0145f9c712073db788a994d62a368759b340ea9" :edb/db-before-t 181 :edb/db-after-t 182 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533494 50 #inst "2026-10-11T02:48:22.405Z" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186064286 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403925 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186078397 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403842 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186087730 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403856 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186087734 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403849 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186087735 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403863 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186087787 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403898 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186092193 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403953 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186092193 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403960 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186096630 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403973 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186096630 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403980 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186096658 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403884 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186096714 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404022 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186100877 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403891 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186100928 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404071 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186100929 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404057 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186105904 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403877 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186115187 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403870 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186115228 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403911 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186115228 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403918 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186115261 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403946 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186124607 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404113 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186124608 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404092 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186124608 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404099 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186124608 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404106 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186129261 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404029 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186133760 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403932 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186133760 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403939 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186147446 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404078 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186147446 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404085 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186147513 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404036 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186147596 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404043 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152175 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404064 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152193 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403987 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152195 1038 #edb/ref 17592186403994 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152195 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404001 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152195 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404008 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152195 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404015 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152781 1068 #edb/ref 17592186151163 13194139533494 17592186045585 false] [17592186152781 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403905 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152781 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152781 1071 "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point $S^{′}$, the image of $S(-4, \\sqrt{3})$ under the action of $T$?" 13194139533494 17592186045585 false] [17592186152781 1071 "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${S}^{′}$, the image of $S(-4,\\sqrt{3})$ under the action of $T?$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152781 1074 "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $S:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${S}^{′}.$ Therefore, ${S}^{′}(15,-1).$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152802 1068 #edb/ref 17592186151289 13194139533494 17592186045585 false] [17592186152802 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403967 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152802 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152802 1071 "![](images/14/14d1fc5a92c28cc7f84c1ec23929701f1aca67b1a15d6113fa83f1428354fc11.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse centered at $(3,-1)$ with horizontal radius $2$ and vertical radius $3$, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $θ ∈ [0, 2π)$, traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(5,-1)$?" 13194139533494 17592186045585 false] [17592186152802 1071 "![](images/14/14d1fc5a92c28cc7f84c1ec23929701f1aca67b1a15d6113fa83f1428354fc11.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse centered at $(3,-1)$ with horizontal radius $2$ and vertical radius $3,$ as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(5,-1)?$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186152802 1074 "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the point $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the ellipse is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(h+a,k).$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(3,-1),$ $a=2$ and $b=3.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186229143 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404050 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403842 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403843 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403842 1069 "q-76374" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403842 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403842 1071 "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n$2{x}^{2}-4x+2{y}^{2}-y=-1.$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403842 1072 #uuid "64257e64-8ece-56eb-a9da-46dae15085ca" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403842 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-4x+2{y}^{2}-y & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}y & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+({y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}y) & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}y+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}) & =-\\frac{1}{2}+{1}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}y+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}) & =\\frac{9}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+{(y-\\frac{1}{4})}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{16} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+{(y-\\frac{1}{4})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(1,\\frac{1}{4})$ and its radius is $\\frac{3}{4}.$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403843 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403844 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403843 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403845 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403843 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403846 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403843 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403847 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403843 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403848 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403843 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403843 1077 "selection" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403843 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403846 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403843 1080 #uuid "64251e03-03e9-594a-89a0-0a7ae7fb1367" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403844 1081 "center: $(1,-\\frac{1}{4}),$ radius: $\\frac{5}{4}$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403844 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403844 1084 #uuid "707a4cfe-d34e-5500-a601-9753b554d97e" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403845 1081 "center: $(-1,-\\frac{1}{4}),$ radius: $\\frac{3}{4}$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403845 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403845 1084 #uuid "0043bbe1-8c13-5357-841d-e795a04df199" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403846 1081 "center: $(1,\\frac{1}{4}),$ radius: $\\frac{3}{4}$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403846 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403846 1084 #uuid "13f05de5-d7d8-5d9c-9e5d-ac75c76fa048" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403847 1081 "center: $(\\frac{1}{4},1),$ radius: $\\frac{7}{4}$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403847 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403847 1084 #uuid "1705b14f-f5fa-5468-b93d-33bcdcdbb387" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403848 1081 "center: $(-1,\\frac{1}{4}),$ radius: $\\frac{5}{4}$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403848 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403848 1084 #uuid "cc1a32ca-3acb-5d7d-b8ad-8a49ebecf6c4" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403849 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403850 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403849 1069 "q-7642" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403849 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403849 1071 "Calculate the points where the ellipse \n$\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{6}=1$ intercepts the $y$-axis." 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403849 1072 #uuid "c9bca935-b9bf-540f-a535-f5de3e3b987f" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403849 1074 "To calculate the $y$-intercept, we need to substitute $x=0$ in the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $y.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ 4+6(y+2)^{2} & =36 \\\\ 6(y+2)^{2} & =32 \\\\ 3(y+2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ (y+2)^{2} & =\\frac{16}{3} \\\\ y+2 & =\\pm \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ y & =-2\\pm \\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $y$-axis at the points $(0,-2-\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3})$ and $(0,-2+\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}).$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403851 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403852 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403853 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403854 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403855 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1077 "selection" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403851 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403850 1080 #uuid "8df721af-644e-5936-b5f6-55c036b03023" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403851 1081 "(0,-2\\pm \\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3})" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403851 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403851 1084 #uuid "4a4e2843-1069-5d5a-bc66-06cba791d839" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403852 1081 "(0,1\\pm \\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3})" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403852 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403852 1084 #uuid "ee8990c4-efb5-5c40-8ee3-12b22397b390" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403853 1081 "(0,2\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2})" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403853 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403853 1084 #uuid "05b80062-5158-567e-9a1e-8cfd58f9c9b1" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403854 1081 "(0,-2\\pm 2\\sqrt{3})" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403854 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403854 1084 #uuid "d7aba08c-b98e-5626-b761-ad0e976d4fab" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403855 1081 "(0,2\\pm \\sqrt{2})" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403855 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403855 1084 #uuid "4d59c083-d711-58a1-a0a9-72a889180cdd" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403856 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403857 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403856 1069 "q-7645" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403856 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403856 1071 "Calculate the points where the ellipse  $9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-36x+16y=-16$ intercepts the $x$-axis." 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403856 1072 #uuid "82249adf-2c55-575e-90cb-7bba0c1d440e" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403856 1074 "To calculate the $x$-intercepts, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-36x+16y & =-16 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}+4(0)^{2}-36x+16(0) & =-16 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-36x & =-16 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x & =-\\frac{16}{9} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}-{2}^{2} & =-\\frac{16}{9} \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =-\\frac{16}{9}+4 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =-\\frac{16}{9}+\\frac{36}{9} \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =\\frac{20}{9} \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3} \\\\ x & =2\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at $(2-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)$ and $(2+\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0).$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403858 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403859 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403860 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403861 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403862 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1077 "selection" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403861 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403857 1080 #uuid "e32446d2-a32e-554b-89ca-512e15fbc942" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403858 1081 "(1\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},0)" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403858 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403858 1084 #uuid "19a9a2f6-bd42-5579-a2ff-e314a223a8b1" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403859 1081 "(1\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403859 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403859 1084 #uuid "85bc7d3a-2417-530a-983c-0a9380f5af4e" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403860 1081 "(-2\\pm 3\\sqrt{2},0)" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403860 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403860 1084 #uuid "57970bb2-2ea8-522d-a5b9-0263776ebf54" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403861 1081 "(2\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403861 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403861 1084 #uuid "7aebdb04-492d-5e2c-828e-8c2f57c1636a" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403862 1081 "(2\\pm \\sqrt{5},0)" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403862 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403862 1084 #uuid "4072ec56-b787-50c7-a9df-ca77f8413053" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403863 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403864 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403863 1069 "q-7646" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403863 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403863 1071 "Determine the points where the ellipse ${x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-4x+4y=10$ intercepts the $y$-axis." 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403863 1072 #uuid "d4ad8b92-e3b5-5a56-bfac-e69e0f571229" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403863 1074 "To calculate the $y$-intercepts, we need to substitute $x=0$ in the equation of the ellipse and try to solve the resulting equation for $y.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-4x+4y & =10 \\\\ (0)^{2}+2{y}^{2}-4(0)+4y & =10 \\\\ 2{y}^{2}+4y & =10 \\\\ {y}^{2}+2y & =5 \\\\ (y+1)^{2}-{1}^{2} & =5 \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =5+1 \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =6 \\\\ y+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{6} \\\\ y & =-1\\pm \\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $y$-axis at $(0,-1-\\sqrt{6})$ and $(0,-1+\\sqrt{6}).