ty ).$ In particular, it is continuous on $[-4,4]$ and differentiable on $(-4,4).$ Therefore, $f(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $g(x)={2}^{1/{x}^{2}}$ is not defined at $x=0,$ hence, it is not continuous at \n$x=0,$ and so it is not continuous on $[-4,4].$ Therefore, $g(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $h(x)=\\sqrt{x+4}$ is continuous on $[-4,\\infty )$ and differentiable on $(-4,\\infty ).$ In particular, it is continuous on $[-4,4]$ and differentiable on $(-4,4).$ Therefore, $h(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only the functions I and III satisfy the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[-4,4].$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403927 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403928 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403929 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403930 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403931 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1077 "selection" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403928 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403926 1080 #uuid "8b1b4626-8500-573c-8ccc-0601d1a1fa54" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403927 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403927 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403927 1084 #uuid "57a0952d-7db5-57ee-878c-0528fe98cbc2" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403928 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403928 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403928 1084 #uuid "d248d05c-c26d-5279-a4c9-650778c4adfc" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403929 1081 "I only" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403929 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403929 1084 #uuid "23471252-b9a8-5480-9786-9004da29f6b9" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403930 1081 "III only" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403930 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403930 1084 #uuid "ac25078c-9c3f-521f-b1bb-d8d1feebcaa7" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403931 1081 "II only" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403931 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403931 1084 #uuid "86791b8f-4a3c-572d-b37b-5531edfec22e" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403932 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403933 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403932 1069 "q-77953" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403932 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403932 1071 "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors ${i,j}$ of ${R}^{2}$ under the action of $T?$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403932 1072 #uuid "6184324c-f65c-5086-93a0-7afae4b6be6a" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403932 1074 "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j}$ are the first and second columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i$ and $T\\cdot j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403933 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403934 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403933 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403935 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403933 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403936 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403933 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403937 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403933 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403938 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403933 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403933 1077 "selection" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403933 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403937 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403933 1080 #uuid "fd1100a3-f46d-5e04-86d4-755b02a479bb" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403934 1081 "$[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403934 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403934 1084 #uuid "50e07024-23d2-5570-be5e-03b114b3c983" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403935 1081 "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403935 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403935 1084 #uuid "e0bbab46-dd35-5c94-a96c-8093cdf108d9" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403936 1081 "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403936 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [1