186403960 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403960 1071 "Consider a system of $n$ linear equations in $n$ variables, written in matrix form as $D\\,t=q.$ Here, $D$ is the non-singular coefficient matrix of the system, $t$ is the column vector containing the variables, and $q$ is the column vector containing the constants. The unique solution of the system can be found using the method shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,t & =q \\\\ \\boxed{\\phantom{D^{-1}}}D\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q \\\\ {I}_{n}\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\,\\boxed{\\phantom{q}} \\\\ t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom and left to right, what are the missing parts of the derivation?" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403960 1072 #uuid "ecf8e0a5-c1dd-5243-9116-de59a516e7ec" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403960 1074 "Since $D$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${D}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $D\\,t=q$ by ${D}^{-1},$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,t & =q \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q \\\\ {I}_{n}\\,t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q \\\\ t & ={D}^{-1}\\,q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts are ${D}^{-1}$ and $q.$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403961 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403962 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403961 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403963 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403961 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403964 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403961 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403965 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403961 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403966 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403961 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403961 1077 "selection" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403961 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403962 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186403961 1080 #uuid "96efe5ef-8066-599a-a9a3-934df32a5fcd" 13194139533494 17592186045585 t