0f-8358-5f70-9dcf-5a12623a7ffa" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404102 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]$ and \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404102 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404102 1084 #uuid "1df643a8-80e1-5748-9179-fabd113dde47" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404103 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]$ and \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404103 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404103 1084 #uuid "0dd75f60-e366-51aa-9704-98e0a480bbc9" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404104 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]$ and \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404104 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404104 1084 #uuid "fa9540b0-0bdb-50eb-99c1-9744cc3a5660" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404105 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ and \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404105 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404105 1084 #uuid "f62ab074-e099-5956-af5c-d32875cc38df" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404106 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404107 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404106 1069 "q-80392" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404106 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404106 1071 "Consider the matrix $B$ for which ${\\lambda }_{1}=5$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3$ are eigenvalues, and\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nare the respective eigenvectors. What are the values of $a,b,c$ given that\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}b & -3 \\\\ c & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}b & -3 \\\\ c & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}?\n$$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404106 1072 #uuid "84388249-87e9-543c-a81f-fd99783cee24" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404106 1074 "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=5$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=5,$ and\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn conclusion, we get  $a=5,$ $b=1,$ and $c=-1.$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404107 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404108 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404107 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404109 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404107 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404110 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404107 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404111 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404107 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404112 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404107 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404107 1077 "selection" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404107 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404108 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404107 1080 #uuid "b352245b-eaa4-5fde-aea9-5afac2d00b93" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404108 1081 "$a=5,$ $b=1,$ and $c=-1$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404108 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404108 1084 #uuid "639780ae-1398-50d7-b815-e2a195a0e73d" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404109 1081 "$a=1,$ $b=-5,$ and $c=-1$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404109 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404109 1084 #uuid "c73ad559-0eae-5f15-bdf7-739e613b69ee" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404110 1081 "$a=1,$ $b=5,$ and $c=-1$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404110 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404110 1084 #uuid "d0038efe-a96a-5281-ad36-c4af7f9c03a2" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404111 1081 "$a=5,$ $b=1,$ and $c=1$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404111 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404111 1084 #uuid "c0406221-3155-5859-8236-e58b9f481700" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404112 1081 "$a=-1,$ $b=1,$ and $c=5$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404112 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404112 1084 #uuid "d939f8e6-1f46-548c-8adc-229c62fd7d9e" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404113 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404114 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404113 1069 "q-80493" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404113 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404113 1071 "Given the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$, \nfind a diagonal matrix $D$ and an invertible matrix $P$ such that $D={P}^{-1}AP.$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404113 1072 #uuid "7be4462e-3d0b-5745-b83e-db8e5d74f57e" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404113 1074 "We apply the diagonalization algorithm.\n\n**Step 1.**  We need to find the eigenvalues of the matrix. Since matrix $A$ is triangular, its eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal: \n\n$\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2$\n\n**Step 2.** Now, we need to find an eigenvector basis of $A.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-3)I & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to its row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $2$nd one). Thus, ${x}_{1}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}=0.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{1}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{1}=1,$ we get the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-2)I & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a homogeneous system of linear equations with the matrix as above. Note, the matrix is already in row echelon form. There is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-2{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3.** We construct the diagonal matrix $D$ and the invertible matrix $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404115 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404116 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404117 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404118 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404119 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404114 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404114 1077 "selection" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404114 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404118 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404114 1080 #uuid "958185d9-bfb3-5c99-9580-566f3546885e" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404115 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404115 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404115 1084 #uuid "15560ba1-c0e7-57a3-bd24-dc19e7e9f52a" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404116 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404116 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404116 1084 #uuid "4a752dce-688f-5fd3-becb-69a53449004c" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404117 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404117 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404117 1084 #uuid "e3bff80f-44fe-590e-825f-851b2661193c" 13194139533494 17592186045585 true] [17592186404118 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0